# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Client environment
#
# ⚠️ YOU ALMOST CERTAINLY DO NOT NEED TO SET ANYTHING IN HERE FOR DEVELOPMENT.
#
# Everything below is commented out on purpose. With no VITE_API_BASE_URL the
# client derives the API origin from whatever host the page was loaded from —
# so localhost calls localhost, and a page served at http://192.168.1.42:3000
# calls http://192.168.1.42:5000. Setting it pins the API to one address and
# turns that off, which is correct for a deployment and wrong for a laptop.
#
# ⚠️ Vite bakes VITE_-prefixed variables in at BUILD TIME, not at server
# runtime like the backend's .env. There is no "set it on the host and
# restart".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── LAN hosting during local development ─────────────────────────────────────
#
#   npm run dev       loopback only — http://localhost:3000
#   npm run dev:lan   also on the Wi-Fi, for testing on a real phone or tablet
#
# `dev:lan` pins port 3000 and prints a "Network:" URL on startup.
# ⚠️ Open THAT URL on the device. `localhost` on a phone means the phone.
#
# Nothing here needs setting for this to work. The API server already listens
# on all interfaces, and CORS accepts private-network origins when NODE_ENV is
# not production (server/src/config/cors.config.ts). In production the
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS allowlist is the only way in — that guard is the safety
# property and must not be softened.
#
# ⚠️ Two things genuinely do NOT work over a plain-HTTP LAN address, because
# browsers withhold them outside a secure context (localhost is exempt):
# microphone capture and clipboard writes. Both screens detect this and say so.
# For real microphone capture on a device, serve over HTTPS or use localhost.
#
# ⚠️ LAN hosting is opt-in per command, not a config default, because this dev
# server renders real seeded patient records behind a real login. Do not run
# `dev:lan` on a café, hotel or client network.


# ── Only set these for a deployed build ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Pins the API origin. Overrides the origin-awareness described above, so leave
# it unset in development.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.your-production-domain.com
#
# Only if the API is NOT on port 5000 of the same host as the page.
# VITE_API_PORT=5000
